==Strategy==
Aside from the nasty Zombie peons, this stage has some of the strongest [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] in the game, therefore it is absolutely crucial to obtain all [[anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] before attempting it. Because the Death Angel Z-Onels can revive infinitely with less than a second between revives, [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] may be needed in order to get past them. Here, the [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] is one of the best [[Cat Cannon|Cannons]] to use for its Zombie Killer and high damage against the Z-Onels, and it is highly recommended to upgrade it as much as possible. At levels 20-30, it damages them for 10-15% of their maximum health (100,000-150,000), which may be enough to land the finishing blow on one of them.

Without high level [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]], the main issue with fighting Z-Onel is accidental overkill and failing to Z-kill at least one of the Z-Onel early on. The strategy is essentially to kill the aliens as fast as possible, then hope to get a lucky Z-kill at least one boss by sneaking the stack in with freeze from Holy Blast. If one of the bosses has been permanently killed, then it is very easy to push Z-Onel all the way to the base and siege it down. As long as the [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] are dealt with 3-4 mins into the fight, then no more will spawn it is relatively easy to keep fighting until the base is destroyed or a Z-kill is achieved.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] - Cadaver BearCat, though hindered by its poor range, deals Insane Damage to Zombies and has Zombie Killer. Many strategies employing this unit seek to stack and sneak them into Death Angel Z-Onel's blindspot (it becomes much more consistent if holy blast/normal cat cannon is used to interrupt Z-Onel) to cripple if not outright destroy them.
*[[Shigong Cat]] - Not as good as Cadaver BearCat but can easily tank Z-Onel and walk into the blind spot reliably.
*[[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]] - Budget version of Cadaver BearCat.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime/Jelly Dumpling Cat]] - Slime Cat has a miniscule amount health, but can generate level 5 wave attacks (level 7 in true form) to whittle down peons and bosses, which given the amount of zombies in this stage can repeatedly occur as they burrow or resurface.
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] - As seen in [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LUgnhCU46No This Video], a LV.50 Royal Guard with the [[Biohazard (Combo)|Bio-]][[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bone]] and [[Mini-Saurus (Combo)|Mini-Saurus]] combos can solo the stage and its [[The Final Corpse (Merciless)|Restriction stage variant.]] You may need a high level Holy Blast, however.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] - Can very reliably wall out the aliens and get inside the blind spot to protect the above Z-killers from subsequent alien spawns.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - A very solid melee option for the peons, outranging all of them while having considerable bulk. Their [[Talents]] make them even better, with Double Bounty, Target Alien and Movement Speed Up adding to their already great stats.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|CAT-8 Behemoth]]: With its insane effective HP against Zombies, CAT-8 Behemoth can at the very least soak up some hits and chip out some damage to Z-Onel. Its Long Distance and [[Wave Attack]]s can also clear out the Zuches (if it happens to hit them), and can do some damage to the other enemies. Don't be fooled by its relatively lackluster performance elsewhere; Behemoth's tankiness can stall the Z-Onels just enough to either finish them off with the Holy Blast if not chip them out themselves.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Celestial Child Luna]]: While her evolved form is poorly equipped to take on Z-Onel, Luna's normal form sees surprising utility here. Her lower ranger allows her to enter Z-Onel's blind spot, and her lowered cost and cooldown is a worthy trade off for her lower chance to activate her freeze.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Used for the rush strategy. Balrog can slip into Z-Onel's blind spot and push her to the base, as well as clear out the peons with relative ease. Can tank two hits at level 30, and being highly disposable with his low recharge time/cost, you can just send another if he is destroyed.
*[[Wrathful Poseidon (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Poseidon]]: Although not the best pick, if you time him correctly, he can deal good damage to the Z-Onels, as well as freezing her, yet he won’t last long because of the starred aliens.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lone Moon Lunos]]: A definitive counter to this stage, as he targets both zombies and aliens. He can tank multiple hits from the peons and Z-onel combined, and his conjure can devastate the enemy's defenses.

